From 574ba3611b76e20df2e22f0391e67beccdf3530a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:12:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gallium/pvr: withdraw EXT_frag_depth and EXT_shadow_samplers
 (unimplemented)

u_init_pipe_screen_caps() defaults two caps to true on the assumption that a driver which does not
clear them supports the feature, and this driver never cleared them:

- caps.fragment_shader_depth makes Mesa advertise GL_EXT_frag_depth, but the fragment variant builder
  has no depth output, so a shader writing gl_FragDepthEXT would be silently ignored.
- caps.texture_shadow_map makes Mesa advertise GL_EXT_shadow_samplers, but the sampler descriptor has
  no compare mode, so comparison sampling would silently sample the raw depth value.

Clear both. The native GLES2 extension list drops from 70 to 68 and matches what the driver can back
(verified with glinfo). GL_EXT_texture_border_clamp/OES_texture_border_clamp cannot be withdrawn this
way - Mesa's extension table marks them dummy_true for ES2 - so they stay advertised and are recorded
as a documented limitation (sampler border colour/wrap support is its own work item).

Verified: gltri 49 modes (all native glGetError 0x0, red 32768), mip gate 28, rttest PASS
(bad=0/262144), rt8test, instancing, extension-texture, half-float-linear tests unchanged, 0 faults.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c
index b46d3b8e..3106ae45 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_screen.c
@@ -310,6 +310,17 @@ pvr_screen_create(int fd, const struct pipe_screen_config *config,
       caps->uma = true;             /* the GPU shares system RAM on this SoC */
       caps->vendor_id = 0x1010;     /* Imagination Technologies PCI vendor ID */
       caps->device_id = ident->device_id;
+
+      /* Two Mesa caps default to true in u_init_pipe_screen_caps() on the assumption that a driver
+       * which does not clear them supports the feature. This one does not: a fragment shader
+       * writing gl_FragDepthEXT would be silently ignored (the variant builder has no depth
+       * output), and comparison sampling has no compare mode in the sampler descriptor. Clearing
+       * the caps withdraws GL_EXT_frag_depth and GL_EXT_shadow_samplers, which is the honest
+       * answer. (Border clamp cannot be withdrawn this way: Mesa's extension table marks it
+       * dummy_true for ES2, so it stays advertised - documented limitation, scoped as a
+       * sampler-border work item.) */
+      caps->fragment_shader_depth = false;
+      caps->texture_shadow_map = false;
    }
 
    /* Runtime info: free-list sizing and the shader limits, which pco needs before it
-- 
